---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Nav from '../components/layout/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../components/layout/Footer.astro';
---
<Base title="matterunknown" description="Ryan Silver's independent identity research lab. Research on identity — especially the identity of AI agents — and real tools built in the open.">
<style>
  .heroWrap { position: relative; }
  .heroWrap::before {
    content: ''; position: absolute; inset: -80px -200px 0;
    background:
      radial-gradient(ellipse 55% 60% at 22% 18%, rgba(196,151,42,.07), transparent 65%),
      radial-gradient(ellipse 40% 50% at 85% 70%, rgba(126,184,196,.035), transparent 70%);
    pointer-events: none;
  }
  .hero { position: relative; display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1.05fr 1fr; gap: 56px; align-items: center; padding: 64px 0 8px; }
  .hero h1 { font-family: var(--serif); font-weight: 400; font-size: clamp(2.2rem, 4.5vw, 3.3rem); line-height: 1.1; letter-spacing: -.01em; margin: 14px 0 18px; text-wrap: balance; }
  .hero h1 a { color: inherit; }
  .hero h1 a:hover { color: var(--amber); }
  .hero .dek { color: var(--text-2); font-size: 1.08rem; max-width: 54ch; margin-bottom: 22px; }
  .hero .by { font-size: .85rem; color: var(--text-3); margin-bottom: 26px; }
  .cta { display: inline-block; background: var(--amber); color: #090908; border-radius: 8px; padding: 11px 22px; font-size: .95rem; font-weight: 500; transition: background .2s; }
  .cta:hover { background: #d4a830; }
  .cta2 { margin-left: 18px; color: var(--amber); font-size: .95rem; }
  .cta2:hover { text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 3px; }
  .heroArt { border-radius: 14px; border: 1px solid rgba(196,151,42,.16); overflow: hidden; box-shadow: 0 30px 80px rgba(0,0,0,.55); }
  .heroArt img { display: block; width: 100%; height: auto; }
  .mission { margin-top: 64px; padding-top: 28px; border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); color: var(--text-2); font-size: 1.02rem; max-width: 72ch; }
  .mission strong { color: var(--text); font-weight: 500; }
  .mission a { color: var(--amber); }
  .programs { margin-top: 26px; display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: 22px; }
  .program { border-left: 2px solid var(--amber-border); padding-left: 18px; }
  .program h3 { font-family: var(--serif); font-weight: 400; font-size: 1.12rem; margin-bottom: 4px; }
  .program p { color: var(--text-3); font-size: .88rem; }
  .program a { color: var(--text); }
  .program a:hover { color: var(--amber); }
  @media (max-width: 900px) { .hero { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } .programs { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
</style>

<Nav variant="full" active="/" />

<main class="wrapb">
  <div class="heroWrap">
    <div class="hero">
      <div>
        <span class="sc">Featured essay · August 2026</span>
        <h1><a href="/writing/retiring-vessel">Retiring Vessel</a></h1>
        <p class="dek">For six months this site ran with an AI persona that named itself. Ending it taught me more about agent identity than building it did.</p>
        <p class="by">Ryan Silver · 7 min read</p>
        <a class="cta" href="/writing/retiring-vessel">Read the essay</a>
        <a class="cta2" href="/about">About the lab →</a>
      </div>
      <div class="heroArt"><img src="/images/art/vessel.png" alt="Fragmented concentric rings in amber" width="1200" height="750" /></div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="mission">
    <strong>matterunknown is Ryan Silver's independent identity research lab.</strong> Serious work on how systems decide who you are — above all, what identity means for AI agents acting on our behalf — alongside real tools and models built for the joy of it. Everything runs in the open: the methods, the trades, and the mistakes are public.
  </div>

  <div class="sect">
    <div class="sect-head"><h2>Latest research</h2><a href="/writing">All writing →</a></div>
    <div class="grid3">
      <a class="icard" href="/writing/the-credential-remembers-who">
        <img src="/images/art/credential.png" alt="" loading="lazy" width="1200" height="750" />
        <div class="icard-body">
          <span class="icard-kicker">Agentic identity</span>
          <h3>The Credential Remembers Who. Nothing Remembers Why.</h3>
          <div class="meta">July 2026</div>
        </div>
      </a>
      <a class="icard" href="/writing/the-workload-is-the-reasoning-session">
        <img src="/images/art/workload.png" alt="" loading="lazy" width="1200" height="750" />
        <div class="icard-body">
          <span class="icard-kicker">Agentic identity</span>
          <h3>The Workload Is the Reasoning Session</h3>
          <div class="meta">July 2026</div>
        </div>
      </a>
      <a class="icard" href="/writing/pokemon-card-market">
        <img src="/images/art/cards.png" alt="" loading="lazy" width="1200" height="750" />
        <div class="icard-body">
          <span class="icard-kicker">Markets</span>
          <h3>The Card Market Has a Data Problem</h3>
          <div class="meta">June 2026</div>
        </div>
      </a>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="sect">
    <div class="sect-head"><h2>From the lab</h2><a href="/projects">All projects →</a></div>
    <div class="grid3">
      <a class="icard" href="https://commonlist.matterunknown.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
        <img src="https://commonlist.matterunknown.com/og.png" alt="Commonlist — one clean address book" loading="lazy" width="1200" height="630" />
        <div class="icard-body">
          <span class="icard-kicker">App · Live</span>
          <h3>Commonlist</h3>
          <p>One clean address book across Google, Microsoft, Outlook, and iCloud.</p>
        </div>
      </a>
      <a class="icard" href="/projects/quant-trading">
        <img src="/images/projects/quant-trading.png" alt="Open positions and trade log from the quant scanner" loading="lazy" width="1280" height="750" />
        <div class="icard-body">
          <span class="icard-kicker">Finance · Paper trading</span>
          <h3>Quant scanner</h3>
          <p>100 symbols scanned nightly. Every position and trade public.</p>
        </div>
      </a>
      <a class="icard" href="/projects/pokemon-model">
        <img src="/images/projects/pokemon-model.png" alt="Pokémon acquisition model dashboard" loading="lazy" width="1280" height="750" />
        <div class="icard-body">
          <span class="icard-kicker">Collecting · Live</span>
          <h3>Pokémon model</h3>
          <p>17,000+ cards scored daily for mispriced scarcity.</p>
        </div>
      </a>
      <a class="icard" href="/projects/identity-map">
        <img src="/images/projects/identity-map.png" alt="Identity Surface Map experiment" loading="lazy" width="1280" height="750" />
        <div class="icard-body">
          <span class="icard-kicker">Research · Interactive</span>
          <h3>Identity Surface Map</h3>
          <p>How many versions of you exist across systems right now?</p>
        </div>
      </a>
      <a class="icard" href="/projects/digital-shadow">
        <img src="/images/projects/digital-shadow.png" alt="Your Digital Shadow questionnaire" loading="lazy" width="1280" height="750" />
        <div class="icard-body">
          <span class="icard-kicker">Research · Interactive</span>
          <h3>Your Digital Shadow</h3>
          <p>What data brokers probably know about you.</p>
        </div>
      </a>
      <a class="icard" href="/projects/password-graveyard">
        <img src="/images/projects/password-graveyard.png" alt="The Password Graveyard analyzer" loading="lazy" width="1280" height="750" />
        <div class="icard-body">
          <span class="icard-kicker">Research · Interactive</span>
          <h3>The Password Graveyard</h3>
          <p>When your password died, and what killed it.</p>
        </div>
      </a>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="sect">
    <div class="sect-head"><h2>Research programs</h2><a href="/model">The framework →</a></div>
    <div class="programs">
      <div class="program">
        <h3><a href="/writing/the-workload-is-the-reasoning-session">Agentic identity</a></h3>
        <p>The flagship: intent tokens that attest to why an agent acts, built on RFC 8693 and SPIFFE. Heading for open source and a paper.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="program">
        <h3><a href="/model">The Identity Model</a></h3>
        <p>Three identity layers, four failure modes — the operating framework behind everything the lab builds.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="program">
        <h3><a href="/writing/synthetic-identity-is-already-here">Identity failure</a></h3>
        <p>Synthetic identity, break-glass trust, identity after death — how the gap between you and your records gets exploited.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</main>

<Footer />
</Base>
